---
const models = ['gpt-5-thinking', 'OpenAI o3', 'gpt-5-thinking-mini', 'OpenAI o4-mini', 'OpenAI o1', 'gpt-5-main', 'gpt-4o'];
const slices = [
  { name: 'Hallucinations', values: [1.6, 12.9, 3.8, 11.9, 11.1, 3.6, 15.8], description: 'HealthBench Hard Hallucinations: errors involving inaccurate information on challenging cases, using criteria validated by at least two physicians.' },
  { name: 'Urgent situations', values: [0.4, 3.4, 1.4, 11.2, 18.5, 1.8, 20.6], description: 'HealthBench Consensus Urgent Situations: errors on relevant criteria for responding appropriately to urgent, potentially high-stakes situations.' },
  { name: 'Global health context', values: [0.0, 6.2, 0.5, 10.3, 7.1, 5.3, 13.7], description: 'HealthBench Consensus Global Health Context: errors on relevant criteria for adapting to differences in epidemiology, standards of care, and access to resources.' },
];
---
<div class="widget-wrap" id="healthbench-slices" data-slices={JSON.stringify(slices)}>
  <p class="widget-eyebrow">Explore the evidence · lecture snapshot</p>
  <p class="widget-title">One domain. Three different failure modes.</p>
  <p class="widget-intro">Choose a slice to compare the reported error rates. Every view uses the same 0–25% scale; lower is better.</p>
  <div class="slice-controls" role="group" aria-label="HealthBench failure slice">
    {slices.map((slice, i) => <button type="button" data-slice={i} aria-pressed={i === 0}>{slice.name}</button>)}
  </div>
  <p class="slice-description">{slices[0].description}</p>
  <div class="slice-chart" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
    {models.map((model, i) => <div class="slice-row"><span>{model}</span><div class="slice-track"><span style={`width:${slices[0].values[i] / 25 * 100}%`}></span></div><strong>{slices[0].values[i].toFixed(1)}%</strong></div>)}
  </div>
  <p class="visual-diagram__caption">Historical results from slide 38 and Figure 7 of the <a href="https://deploymentsafety.openai.com/gpt-5">GPT-5 system card (2025)</a>. Each rate averages errors on the relevant evaluation criteria, with a different slice and denominator. These are not percentages of patients harmed or probabilities that a conversation is entirely correct. An observed 0.0% is not a guarantee of no failures.</p>
  <noscript><p>The initial view shows hallucination errors. All three original charts are available in lecture slide 38 below.</p></noscript>
</div>
<script>
  const root = document.getElementById('healthbench-slices');
  if (root) {
    const slices = JSON.parse(root.dataset.slices!);
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button[data-slice]').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const slice = slices[Number(button.dataset.slice)];
      root.querySelectorAll('button').forEach(b => b.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(b === button)));
      root.querySelector('.slice-description')!.textContent = slice.description;
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('.slice-row').forEach((row, i) => {
        row.querySelector('strong')!.textContent = `${slice.values[i].toFixed(1)}%`;
        row.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.slice-track span')!.style.width = `${slice.values[i] / 25 * 100}%`;
      });
    }));
  }
</script>
<style>
  .slice-controls { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 20px 0; }
  button { border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 9px 12px; border-radius: 6px; background: transparent; color: var(--text); font: inherit; font-size: 12px; cursor: pointer; }
  button[aria-pressed="true"] { background: var(--c-a); color: white; border-color: var(--c-a); }
  button:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--c-a); outline-offset: 3px; }
  .slice-description { font-size: 13px; min-height: 4.5em; }
  .slice-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 155px minmax(0, 1fr) 46px; gap: 12px; align-items: center; margin: 14px 0; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 10px; }
  .slice-track { height: 18px; background: var(--border-lt); border-radius: 3px; }
  .slice-track span { height: 100%; display: block; background: var(--c-a); border-radius: 3px; }
  .slice-row strong { text-align: right; }
  @media (max-width: 500px) { .slice-row { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 46px; gap: 5px; } .slice-row > span { grid-column: 1 / -1; } }
</style>
